{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790959046,"nonce":"vJaOFFuBL9JYE+nWdLJOw1z2VE4=","title":"A deferred library shell's direct callees are not lowered when they are hooks the program supplies","message":"With defer_prelowered_bodies, adopt_prelowered_reached adopts a linked function as a signature shell. calls_with_nowhere_to_land has no instructions to scan in a shell, and a callee that is a program-supplied hook already has an extern shell in the module, so the ordinary owed-body pass skips it. The hook's body is never lowered: every Python conformance category fails with \"unknown function 'zb_hook_shaped_getslice'\" (and similar hooks) at 4757bfb5.\n\nFix: when deferring, carry the split-module directory's direct-callee targets of each adopted shell into owed_targets, so a hook the program supplies gets its body. Regression: prelowered_linking a_body_replacing_a_linked_extern_has_its_dependencies_adopted, run with deferral on and off.","files":null}]}